<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62875" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λήϊτον</span></b> , τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαός, λεώς</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>town-hall, council-chamber</i>, as the Achaeans of
			Achaea Phthiotis called it, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.197
			</span></i>; 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημόσιον</span>
			 acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Rom.</u>
				26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.280a
			</span></i>:—<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> has <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάϊτον:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀρχεῖον</span>, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαΐτων:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν δημοσίων τόπων</span>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαιετόν, λαῖστρον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Zonar.
			</span></i>:—<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> also quotes <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ληΐτη</span></b> ,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῃτή</span></b> , 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱέρεια</span>
			, a <i>public priestess.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
